  "overview": {
    "text": "The sine function, written sin θ, assigns a number to an angle θ. For an acute angle in a right triangle, sine is the length of the opposite side divided by the hypotenuse. The function also applies to any real angle: if the angle’s terminal side meets the unit circle at (x, y), then sin θ is y, the point’s vertical coordinate. This connects triangle ratios with rotations and extends sine beyond right-triangle angles. As θ changes, sine repeats every 2π radians (360°) and stays between −1 and 1, producing its familiar wave-shaped graph. These properties make sine useful for finding unknown lengths and representing repeating patterns.",
    "source_urls": [
      "https://mathbooks.unl.edu/PreCalculus/sine-and-cosine.html",
      "https://openstax.org/books/precalculus-2e/pages/5-4-right-triangle-trigonometry",
      "https://openstax.org/books/precalculus-2e/pages/6-1-graphs-of-the-sine-and-cosine-functions"
    ]
  },
  "key_facts": [
    {
      "text": "In a right triangle, sin θ = opposite side ÷ hypotenuse.",
      "source_urls": [
        "https://mathbooks.unl.edu/PreCalculus/sine-and-cosine.html"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "On the unit circle, sin θ is the y-coordinate of the point corresponding to the angle.",
      "source_urls": [
        "https://mathbooks.unl.edu/PreCalculus/sine-and-cosine.html"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The standard sine function has domain all real numbers and range [−1, 1].",
      "source_urls": [
        "https://openstax.org/books/precalculus-2e/pages/6-1-graphs-of-the-sine-and-cosine-functions"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Sine repeats every 2π radians, or 360°.",
      "source_urls": [
        "https://openstax.org/books/precalculus-2e/pages/6-1-graphs-of-the-sine-and-cosine-functions"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Because sine tracks the unit-circle y-coordinate, its value is positive above the x-axis and negative below it.",
      "source_urls": [
        "https://mathbooks.unl.edu/PreCalculus/sine-and-cosine.html"
      ]
    }
  ],
